                <pb facs="0555" n="546" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg546"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.6341 South American Development Co./52:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Ecuador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gade</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-02T12:00:00-05:00">February 2,
                        1938—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 4:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>14. Department’s telegram No. 7, February 1, 7 p.m. Rivas, the South American
                    Development Company’s local agent, this morning <pb facs="0556" n="547"
                        xml:id="pg547"/> interviewed General Enriquez who declared that he could not
                    grant a formal extension but would give an informal extension until February 5,
                    noon, until which time he promised that no action will be taken by the
                    Government. I am therefore making no representations pending further
                    instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gade</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
